                                                        <rect key="frame" x="20" y="20" width="353" height="20"/>
                                                        <constraints>
                                                            <constraint firstAttribute="height" constant="20" id="cBy-XM-DIq"/>
                                                        </constraints>
                                                        <fontDescription key="fontDescription" type="system" pointSize="17"/>
                                                        <color key="textColor" red="0.42882183190000001" green="0.41974490879999998" blue="0.68238306049999997" alpha="1" colorSpace="custom" customColorSpace="displayP3"/>
                                                        <nil key="highlightedColor"/>
                                                    </label>
                                                    <label opaque="NO" userInteractionEnabled="NO" contentMode="left" horizontalHuggingPriority="251" verticalHuggingPriority="251" textAlignment="natural" lineBreakMode="wordWrap" numberOfLines="0" baselineAdjustment="alignBaselines" adjustsFontSizeToFit="NO" translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints="NO" id="Sg1-gQ-aN3" customClass="FontLL15" customModule="CalmscientIOS" customModuleProvider="target">
                                                        <rect key="frame" x="20" y="60" width="353" height="300"/>
                                                        <constraints>
                                                            <constraint firstAttribute="height" constant="300" id="RDW-SI-c3V"/>
                                                        </constraints>
                                                        <string key="text">Most teens who smoke think they will quit in their 20s and actually don't until their 40s. Stopping smoking is about making a change and that is something we're not too good at, in fact smoking cessation can be a long journey of trying and relapsing, just like a long ride on a roller coaster. There is no magic solution or medication to transform one to a non-smoker overnight, though some people have the gene to be able to quit smoking or drinking without any struggles.


So what does this ride of change look like? There are 4 steps and helpful strategies you can take!</string>
                                                        <fontDescription key="fontDescription" type="system" pointSize="17"/>
                                                        <nil key="textColor"/>
                                                        <nil key="highlightedColor"/>
                                                    </label>
